# Frontend Figma + Responsive Rule

- Use this Figma as the primary component/style reference for UI work:
  - https://www.figma.com/design/KGMKr1LvtObELhepvaYeOI/Free-Dark-Admin-Dashboards--Community-?node-id=4928-53271&p=f&t=Cffq2aMx7gf0z8ys-0
- Build UI components to match the Figma structure, spacing rhythm, typography scale, and visual hierarchy.
- All new and updated UI must be responsive by default.
- Do not ship fixed-width layouts for page-level containers or core interactive components.

## Responsive baseline

- Mobile-first styling.
- Support at least these breakpoints:
  - mobile: `< 768px`
  - tablet: `768px - 1023px`
  - desktop: `>= 1024px`
- Ensure key screens remain usable at narrow widths without horizontal scrolling.
- Keep touch targets and form controls comfortably usable on mobile.

## PR/check expectations

- For UI changes, include quick verification notes for mobile, tablet, and desktop behavior.
- If a Figma element is intentionally deviated from, document the reason in the change notes.
